{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>I will not see your face again</b> — another time, after I depart. For at the plague of the firstborn he did not see him, since the reason for \"and he called for Moses and Aaron\" (Exodus 12:31) is that he went to the entrance of their house and cried out in the darkness, \"Rise up, get out from among my people\" (ibid.). Or he sent to them through the Egyptians, for it is said of them (ibid. 33), \"and the Egyptians pressed hard upon the people to hasten to send them out of the land.\" And it is possible that he means <b>I will not see your face again</b> — in your palace; that I will not come to you anymore. And thus they said in Shemot Rabbah: \"Well said! Do not see my face anymore — I am not coming to you; you are coming to me.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The verse quotations from Pharaoh's words in midrash reflect the dialogic context; Ramban cites the midrash's rendering where Pharaoh's own words are turned back, preserving the original Hebrew forms."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:05:46.442725862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}